For my design, I wanted to ensure both hardware stability and a precise user experience.
On the hardware side, I designed the buttons with pull-down resistors so the Arduino gets a clean, stable signal without any random bouncing or interference.
On the software side, I designed the logic around State Change Detection. I structured it so that exactly one click equals one count (+1 or -1). Even if a user
long-presses or holds the button down, the system is designed to ignore it and prevent it from counting fast. It forces the counter to wait until the button is 
fully released and clicked again, making the interface completely precise and reliable.
